; hbnf config grammar, as an ASTBNF schema over the token stream.
;
; Built-in core types (interpreted by the codegen, never part of the grammar):
;   str   = a quoted c-string      atom  = a bare token (symbol or number)
;   int / dec / float / bool / flag / u8..u64 / i8..i64 = typed atoms.
;
; hbnf AST nodes map to these rules: Directive -> statement, Block -> block.
; Word -> atom, Str -> str, Int -> int, Dec -> dec.  An entry ends with ";"
; (optional) and is separated from the next by `ws` — one or more newlines
; and comments, which are whitespace exactly as hbnf's own parser treats them.

config    = [ws] *( entry [semicolon] [ws] ) [ws]
entry     = block / statement
statement = name *arg
block     = name [qualifier] "{" [ws] *( entry [semicolon] [ws] ) [ws] "}"
name      = atom
qualifier = str / atom
arg       = atom / str / int / dec
ws        = 1*( "\n" / comment )
semicolon = ";"
